WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.634 --> 00:00:02.667
-Welcome back to "Late Night."
We're here with Woody Harrelson.

00:00:02.667 --> 00:00:04.000
So, this is
a fantastic new film.

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:05.701
And from the clip,
we can see there's a lot

00:00:05.701 --> 00:00:07.834
of actors with
intellectual disabilities,

00:00:07.834 --> 00:00:11.133
and many of whom, obviously,
you've never met before.

00:00:11.133 --> 00:00:14.367
Is it true that the first time
you met them was the scene

00:00:14.367 --> 00:00:16.067
where you met them in the film?

00:00:16.067 --> 00:00:19.701
-Yeah. Yeah, Bobby Farrelly,
who directed it --

00:00:19.701 --> 00:00:24.467
you know, it is a comedic
masterpiece, which, you know,

00:00:24.467 --> 00:00:27.100
the last time we did
a film together was "Kingpin,"

00:00:27.100 --> 00:00:28.701
another comedic masterpiece.

00:00:28.701 --> 00:00:31.400
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:35.434
Anyway, he had said
the night before --

00:00:35.434 --> 00:00:37.934
he arranged that
to happen like that.

00:00:37.934 --> 00:00:39.868
But he had said, "Listen,
you know, we're going to try

00:00:39.868 --> 00:00:43.000
to get the scene, but you never
know how things are gonna work.

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:45.434
We might end up throwing
the script out all together."

00:00:45.434 --> 00:00:46.767
I break out into a sweat.

00:00:46.767 --> 00:00:48.901
I'm like what the f-- heck.

00:00:48.901 --> 00:00:51.667
[ Laughter ]

00:00:51.667 --> 00:00:54.067
I forgot, network television.

00:00:54.067 --> 00:00:55.734
[ Laughter ]

00:00:55.734 --> 00:00:57.734
Yeah, no. So, I was --

00:00:57.734 --> 00:01:00.300
I got very worried about that
because I'm used

00:01:00.300 --> 00:01:03.634
to the context of a script,
and improvising may be inside

00:01:03.634 --> 00:01:05.100
of that, but this --

00:01:05.100 --> 00:01:07.000
anyway, there was no need
to worry.

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:10.367
I came in.
These guys were just so fun.

00:01:10.367 --> 00:01:13.367
And they would come up
with great improvs,

00:01:13.367 --> 00:01:16.434
and the whole experience
was just joyful.

00:01:16.434 --> 00:01:17.968
And I don't know, I guess --

00:01:17.968 --> 00:01:21.133
we call them the friends
in the movie,

00:01:21.133 --> 00:01:24.434
and the friends, they speak
the language of the heart,

00:01:24.434 --> 00:01:27.501
and that is definitely
a language that I dig.

00:01:27.501 --> 00:01:29.501
-Yeah.
They're very -- they come off --

00:01:29.501 --> 00:01:32.501
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:32.501 --> 00:01:36.501
They come off in a really
genuine, authentic way

00:01:36.501 --> 00:01:39.400
that a lot of professional
actors have trouble doing.

00:01:39.400 --> 00:01:40.667
You know what I mean?

00:01:40.667 --> 00:01:42.534
You're watching them and you
just get a sense of this

00:01:42.534 --> 00:01:44.400
is just coming right out of
them, just flowing through them.

00:01:44.400 --> 00:01:46.100
-Right, right.
-Really nice to see.

00:01:46.100 --> 00:01:48.567
-Yeah.
-You and Bobby --

00:01:48.567 --> 00:01:50.434
So you worked on "Kingpin"
together,

00:01:50.434 --> 00:01:51.834
but you've known each other
forever.

00:01:51.834 --> 00:01:53.601
I did not realize you went
way back.

00:01:53.601 --> 00:01:56.167
-Literally within the first
week I moved to L.A.,

00:01:56.167 --> 00:01:59.701
when I was 23, I met Bobby
and Pete, his brother.

00:01:59.701 --> 00:02:03.300
-And I want to talk about
your long history together,

00:02:03.300 --> 00:02:04.734
but I did not know
this, as well --

00:02:04.734 --> 00:02:07.968
You and Bobby had some --
before you made great films,

00:02:07.968 --> 00:02:09.400
inventions.

00:02:09.400 --> 00:02:11.467
You had some ideas for
money-making adventures.

00:02:11.467 --> 00:02:13.434
-Now, you really have done
your research.

00:02:13.434 --> 00:02:14.767
-Yeah, well --

00:02:14.767 --> 00:02:17.667
-Because I thought that was
buried ancient history.

00:02:17.667 --> 00:02:21.267
-I read a lot of
inventor magazines.

00:02:21.267 --> 00:02:23.601
-We did have
an incredible invention,

00:02:23.601 --> 00:02:26.467
and it was 6-foot round
beach towel,

00:02:26.467 --> 00:02:29.167
so now when the sun moves,
your towel doesn't have to.

00:02:29.167 --> 00:02:33.734
[ Laughter ]

00:02:33.734 --> 00:02:36.133
So that -- that went huge.

00:02:36.133 --> 00:02:37.501
That went huge.

00:02:37.501 --> 00:02:39.501
-I think we all remember
that summer where everybody

00:02:39.501 --> 00:02:40.667
had a giant circular towel.

00:02:40.667 --> 00:02:42.701
-Everyone had the circle.

00:02:42.701 --> 00:02:44.067
-How far did you guys
take your --

00:02:44.067 --> 00:02:46.100
Did you ever march on down
to the patent office

00:02:46.100 --> 00:02:47.868
with your circular-towel idea?

00:02:47.868 --> 00:02:49.968
-We did.
-Yeah.

00:02:49.968 --> 00:02:54.033
-But, unfortunately,
that didn't make revenue.

00:02:54.033 --> 00:02:55.934
[ Laughter ]

00:02:55.934 --> 00:02:57.801
You know, it was a great idea,

00:02:57.801 --> 00:03:00.234
but we didn't quite get her
across the finish line.

00:03:00.234 --> 00:03:01.400
-That's all right.

00:03:01.400 --> 00:03:03.033
You know what?
You've had your other successes.

00:03:03.033 --> 00:03:05.534
And I wouldn't hold on to that
failure too much, you know?

00:03:05.534 --> 00:03:07.334
-You're right.
I mean, I should just let go

00:03:07.334 --> 00:03:10.067
of that and just focus
on the good [bleep]

00:03:10.067 --> 00:03:11.734
Yeah, totally.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:11.734 --> 00:03:16.534
-So, now, you were living
with both Farrellys after --

00:03:16.534 --> 00:03:18.334
even after you got cast
in "Cheers"?

00:03:18.334 --> 00:03:21.067
-I lived with Pete.
He and I were roommates.

00:03:21.067 --> 00:03:23.901
But poor Pete, you know,
before they did

00:03:23.901 --> 00:03:26.100
"Dumb and Dumber"...
-Yeah, that was their breakout.

00:03:26.100 --> 00:03:29.200
-And then Bobby and I
were working together.

00:03:29.200 --> 00:03:30.901
But we were
seeing each other all the time.

00:03:30.901 --> 00:03:34.033
We were all such good friends
and a bunch of other

00:03:34.033 --> 00:03:36.133
really funny friends of theirs
from Rhode Island.

00:03:36.133 --> 00:03:43.567
Anyway, Pete and I, he wanted me
to do "Dumb and Dumber."

00:03:43.567 --> 00:03:46.133
Talk about --
How about dumbest, right?

00:03:46.133 --> 00:03:48.434
[ Laughter ]

00:03:48.434 --> 00:03:51.267
-If you had "Dumb, Dumber,
and Dumbest," I would do that.

00:03:51.267 --> 00:03:53.100
But what I did, I said,
"Petey --"

00:03:53.100 --> 00:03:54.834
Now, Petey's a real good
pool player,

00:03:54.834 --> 00:03:57.534
and I fancy myself
as not bad, either.

00:03:57.534 --> 00:04:01.634
Anyway, so, I said,
"Petey, I'll tell you what.

00:04:01.634 --> 00:04:04.901
I'm kind of torn.
Let's play a game of pool.

00:04:04.901 --> 00:04:07.267
And if I win,
I'm not gonna do it.

00:04:07.267 --> 00:04:09.100
If you win, I'll do it."

00:04:09.100 --> 00:04:11.868
So, it came down to the 8 ball,
right?

00:04:11.868 --> 00:04:17.367
And it's like a shot that's
an insane slice shot

00:04:17.367 --> 00:04:19.868
into the pocket that --
you know, most people --

00:04:19.868 --> 00:04:22.834
even Willie Mosconi
would have had trouble.

00:04:22.834 --> 00:04:25.067
Me, I sink that damn ball.

00:04:25.067 --> 00:04:30.100
[ Laughter ]

00:04:30.100 --> 00:04:32.367
-Was he kind enough to remind
you about that over the years?

00:04:32.367 --> 00:04:34.501
-Holy [bleep]

00:04:34.501 --> 00:04:36.767
I don't need any reminder
about that one.

00:04:36.767 --> 00:04:38.701
[ Laughter ]
Yeah.

00:04:38.701 --> 00:04:42.667
It's like one of the great
comedies of all time.

00:04:42.667 --> 00:04:45.367
-Well, again, you know,
you got that,

00:04:45.367 --> 00:04:46.734
you got circular towel,

00:04:46.734 --> 00:04:48.000
but otherwise, I think
they've all been hits.

00:04:48.000 --> 00:04:49.968
-Let those go, let those go!
-Yeah, let those go!

00:04:49.968 --> 00:04:51.567
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:51.567 --> 00:04:54.067
-Hey, man, it's always
such a pleasure to see you.

00:04:54.067 --> 00:04:55.634
-Yes, Seth, very special.
-Congratulations on everything.

00:04:55.634 --> 00:04:57.334
-Good to see you.
-Woody Harrelson.

00:04:57.334 --> 00:04:59.434
"Champions" premieres
in theaters on March 10th.

00:04:59.434 --> 00:05:01.300
We'll be right back
with Niall Horan.

